tls_client.zig is a modified copy of lib/std/crypto/tls/Client.zig from the Zig 0.17.0 standard
library, which is licensed under the MIT License (Expat), Copyright (c) Zig contributors.

Why it is vendored: std.http.Client verifies the server certificate during the TLS handshake but does
not expose it, and superfeedreader's monitor must record certificate expiry. The patch (marked
"[sfr patch]") adds two things only: Options.host = .sni_only (send SNI, skip verification) and
Options.leaf_not_after (receive the leaf certificate's notAfter). Nothing else is changed, and the
probe is never used to establish trust; actual requests still go through std.http.Client, which verifies.

When upgrading Zig: re-copy the upstream file and re-apply the marked changes.
